<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Rhos</h1><p class="st-meta">450 CE – 900 CE (approx.) · capital Deganwy</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Early kingdom of the north Welsh coast east of the Conwy, guarded by the fortress of Deganwy, which became a cantref of Gwynedd.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Rhos lay between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-conwy">River Conwy</a> and the Clwydian hills, on the coast of modern Conwy county. Welsh tradition linked it with the sons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cunedda">Cunedda</a>, and in the 6th century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gildas">Gildas</a> denounced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuneglasus">Cuneglasus</a>, often identified as a king of Rhos, as the charioteer of the Bear's Stronghold, possibly the hillfort of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bryn-euryn">Bryn Euryn</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colwyn-bay">Colwyn Bay</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deganwy">Deganwy</a>, on twin hills above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-conwy">Conwy</a> estuary, was associated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maelgwn-gwynedd">Maelgwn Gwynedd</a> and with the rulers of Rhos, and excavation has found imported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> pottery of the 5th and 6th centuries. The kingdom was closely tied to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-gwynedd">Kingdom of Gwynedd</a> and its kings were probably a junior branch of Maelgwn's dynasty.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 822, according to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/annales-cambriae">Annales Cambriae</a>, the Mercians destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deganwy">Deganwy</a> and took control of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-powys">Powys</a>. Rhos was later firmly part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-gwynedd">Kingdom of Gwynedd</a> as a cantref of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perfeddwlad">Perfeddwlad</a>, contested with English kings, until the conquest of 1283.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-rhos.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Rhos" width="320" height="335"><figcaption>Image: author of source image, plus my additions (myself) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wales.post-Roman.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>450 CE – 900 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Deganwy</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Cuneglasus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Welsh</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Rhos</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=675&amp;focus=kingdom-of-rhos" aria-label="Kingdom of Rhos on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4597 345 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Rhos lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4917 601L4912 613"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4912 613h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4917 601h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4917 601h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=675&amp;focus=kingdom-of-rhos">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

